1
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:06,120
Taming The Husband

2
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:08,720
Episode 9

3
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,120
Madam, please let me go!

4
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:15,120
I've learned my manners.
I won't disgrace the family.

5
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,040
I promise.

6
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:21,760
The Xie family
The Su family

7
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:29,320
Grain Transport Wharf

8
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:31,760
The Yang family
The Xie family

9
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:33,800
The incense has burned out!

10
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:36,040
The Bai family, 30 sacks.

11
00:01:36,440 --> 00:01:38,120
The Xie family, 21 sacks.

12
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:40,120
The Su family, 19 sacks.

13
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:42,320
The Su family is eliminated.

14
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:46,960
Good! Good! Good! Good!

15
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:48,440
Good!

16
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:49,560
Good!

17
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:07,480
Be careful, all of you.

18
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:17,520
If only she knew how to fight.

19
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:19,040
Don't get ahead of yourself.

20
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:20,120
Focus on what's in front of you.

21
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:21,200
Who asked you?

22
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:26,320
The third contest is Seize the Prize.

23
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:30,400
Climb the poles and take the ball.

24
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:32,800
Each family sends four people.

25
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:34,360
There's no time limit.

26
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:38,640
The first to bring the ball ashore wins.

27
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:41,000
If you fall to the ground,

28
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:44,400
you're out of the contest.

29
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:54,320
Everyone, gather around.

30
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:55,640
Listen.

31
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:57,600
Here's our plan.

32
00:02:58,400 --> 00:02:59,400
You're a Xie, too?

33
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:02,280
What's the big deal?
What's there to discuss?

34
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:05,440
Junmei, what are they doing?

35
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:07,840
Putting on a show. Ignore them.

36
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,640
Just do as I told you.

37
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:24,400
Begin!

38
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:25,720
Grain Transport Wharf

39
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:32,920
Yi, you and Bai Junmei
are the best fighters,

40
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:34,320
and you've still got plenty of strength.

41
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:35,400
You're the top horses.

42
00:03:35,760 --> 00:03:38,880
Your job is to beat their middle horse,
Huang Yulan.

43
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:41,400
My old injury's back. I'm exhausted.

44
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:44,080
That makes me our weakest horse.
I'll keep Bai Junmei occupied.

45
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:47,720
Qiao, reach the top
in seven and a half minutes.

46
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:50,120
Shake off their weakest horse
and take the prize.

47
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:00,600
Lose today. There's always tomorrow.

48
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:02,400
Your back injury still hasn't healed.

49
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:04,000
That bright future of yours

50
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:05,480
could be ruined for good.

51
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:11,680
You'll stop at nothing.

52
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:14,160
Not long left to live, have you?

53
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:30,440
Heng!

54
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:35,200
Heng!

55
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:36,720
Go and see if he's hurt!

56
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:39,120
What are you waiting for?

57
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:41,000
Hurry!

58
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:53,720
Never mind me. Keep looking ahead!

59
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:56,920
You've already used up a lot of strength.

60
00:04:57,080 --> 00:04:58,080
Still got any fight left?

61
00:04:58,760 --> 00:05:00,160
Stop barking at me!

62
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:01,760
Get him!

63
00:05:10,320 --> 00:05:11,320
Who are you?

64
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:13,680
Your worst nightmare!

65
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:16,760
This… this is madness!

66
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,720
Someone! Get her down!

67
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:20,360
Uncle, I sent her.

68
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:22,440
You… just look at that son of yours!

69
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:25,520
Losing is one thing.
But she could be killed!

70
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:27,760
Taking a risk
beats sitting here waiting to lose.

71
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:30,040
Sit down, all of you!

72
00:05:30,320 --> 00:05:31,320
But--

73
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:34,640
Panicking like this is a disgrace!

74
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:37,520
Get him!
Give him everything you've got!

75
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:39,800
We're just having a friendly match.

76
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:42,080
Why take it so personally, miss?

77
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:55,760
You?

78
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:57,840
Me.

79
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:04,200
All show, no strength.

80
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:05,320
You'll never make it.

81
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:08,880
Are you afraid of heights?

82
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Watch out!

83
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:17,400
Jianwei!

84
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:18,480
I'm here.

85
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:21,680
Chilly up there, isn't it?

86
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:52,520
Left foot, right foot.

87
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:56,280
Left, right.

88
00:06:57,320 --> 00:06:59,120
Left, right.

89
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:01,520
Putting on a show.

90
00:07:04,240 --> 00:07:06,000
Left, right. Left, right.

91
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:07,080
Left, right.

92
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:09,440
<i>Lift your left foot, then your right.</i>

93
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:11,640
<i>Walk faster and faster.</i>
<i>Faster and faster.</i>

94
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:13,560
<i>Run faster and faster.</i>
<i>Faster and faster.</i>

95
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:14,760
Careful!

96
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:22,400
<i>Suddenly, he swings a punch at you.</i>

97
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:24,640
<i>You dodge quickly,</i>
<i>left and right, with quick little steps,</i>

98
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:26,000
<i>and avoid the blow.</i>

99
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:30,520
Are you mad?

100
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:32,680
It's an embroidered ball!
Is it worth dying for?

101
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:36,320
My life's worth nothing anyway!

102
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:42,680
<i>Plant your feet,</i>

103
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:49,240
<i>lift your leg,</i>
<i>and kick, again and again!</i>

104
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:54,200
Catch the rope!

105
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:07,720
Baozhu,
show them how much of this world

106
00:08:07,840 --> 00:08:10,320
they still know nothing about!

107
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:17,440
Junmei!

108
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:32,520
Full Granaries

109
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:44,320
Baozhu!

110
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,000
Someone help!

111
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:04,360
Young Master Xie's on his feet!

112
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:08,240
Am I seeing things?

113
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:10,040
He really is standing!

114
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:12,640
His legs are better!

115
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:15,440
My lord!

116
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:16,960
Stay back!

117
00:09:57,320 --> 00:09:59,120
She's out! She's safe!

118
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:33,240
The Bai family
The Xie family

119
00:11:09,120 --> 00:11:10,120
Good work.

120
00:11:35,280 --> 00:11:36,320
The Bai family
The Xie family

121
00:11:41,840 --> 00:11:44,400
At this year's shipping festival,

122
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:47,120
the Xies are our champions!

123
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:50,280
Here is Yangzhou Prefecture's decree.

124
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:53,480
From this day on,
between Yangzhou and the capital,

125
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:57,520
all priority government grain shipments

126
00:11:57,920 --> 00:12:01,280
will be handled solely by the Xie family.

127
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:02,560
Good!

128
00:12:02,640 --> 00:12:04,880
We thank His Majesty for his favor.

129
00:12:05,040 --> 00:12:06,040
-Good!
-Good!

130
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:18,080
My lord!

131
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:21,040
The contest's over!
Why are you still hitting people?

132
00:12:21,480 --> 00:12:22,720
-I…
-You…

133
00:12:22,800 --> 00:12:25,720
-You…
-Shameless! You filthy cheat!

134
00:12:27,520 --> 00:12:28,520
Are you all right, my lord?

135
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:30,720
Baozhu. Enough.

136
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,640
Get changed, before you catch a cold.

137
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:36,040
Junmei, are you all right?

138
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:37,640
You…

139
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:49,920
The Xie estate

140
00:12:50,320 --> 00:12:52,520
Yesterday, Xie Yan was calling in debts.

141
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:53,920
Today he's on his feet.

142
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:56,600
And tomorrow,
he'll want a slice of our business!

143
00:12:57,520 --> 00:13:00,520
We're one family.
His success is ours, too.

144
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:03,600
We each have our own household.

145
00:13:03,920 --> 00:13:06,080
Even brothers keep separate accounts.

146
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:09,080
Qiao only handles odd jobs at the docks.

147
00:13:09,840 --> 00:13:12,120
Yi works the short routes with me.

148
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:14,000
He can still get some

149
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:15,320
private allowance out of me.

150
00:13:16,040 --> 00:13:18,160
At least I have a son, too.

151
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:20,120
And mine works the long routes!

152
00:13:20,520 --> 00:13:23,680
But now here comes Xie Yan!

153
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:25,920
How am I supposed to compete?

154
00:13:27,520 --> 00:13:30,840
Tell me, you couldn't even give me a son!

155
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:33,360
Are you sure it's my fault and not yours?

156
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:34,600
Hard to say, isn't it?

157
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:36,000
Enough, enough!

158
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:37,600
Honestly!

159
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:42,280
You only see that he has two sons.

160
00:13:42,640 --> 00:13:45,320
But you take all the money
from the short routes and the docks.

161
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:48,320
Your brother-in-law
only has the long routes.

162
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:49,520
Of course he'd want his share.

163
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:51,720
If he hadn't come back to Yangzhou,

164
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,720
I'd have the long routes, too!

165
00:13:55,560 --> 00:13:57,920
What was Mother thinking,
making such a mess of things?

166
00:13:59,040 --> 00:14:00,720
She sent Heng off on the ships

167
00:14:01,680 --> 00:14:03,720
and put his two sons under me instead.

168
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,640
Now it's all a mess!

169
00:14:06,880 --> 00:14:08,320
You help each other
and keep each other honest.

170
00:14:08,920 --> 00:14:10,280
That's not such a bad thing.

171
00:14:10,520 --> 00:14:11,800
Not bad?

172
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:14,440
Now he's sent another son over!

173
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:16,520
How are we supposed to compete?

174
00:14:17,520 --> 00:14:19,160
If Heng married someone in the trade,

175
00:14:19,240 --> 00:14:21,520
I'd get a few more routes.

176
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,200
But Heng simply won't marry!

177
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:26,920
Every branch has its own interests.

178
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:29,280
And within each branch,
people have their own interests, too.

179
00:14:29,680 --> 00:14:30,920
No need to rush.

180
00:14:31,880 --> 00:14:33,880
Someone else is more worried than we are.

181
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:36,360
Heng! I'm off.

182
00:14:46,800 --> 00:14:48,080
Heng! Heng!

183
00:14:48,640 --> 00:14:49,640
You…

184
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:56,760
Quiet virtue brings good fortune

185
00:14:56,840 --> 00:14:58,400
Come on, come on, come on.
Let's raise our cups

186
00:14:58,480 --> 00:15:00,680
to the Xies reclaiming the title!

187
00:15:01,120 --> 00:15:02,280
Congratulations! Congratulations, sir!

188
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:03,600
Congratulations to the Xie family!

189
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:07,960
Yan.

190
00:15:13,040 --> 00:15:14,040
Here, Yan.

191
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:16,520
Have some more.

192
00:15:18,040 --> 00:15:19,120
I don't like fish.

193
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:25,840
Then… let's have a drink, just you and me.

194
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:26,920
I don't drink, either.

195
00:15:29,440 --> 00:15:30,440
Yan,

196
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:32,600
Father's put together
all this food and wine for you.

197
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:34,000
What's with the attitude?

198
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:35,440
If you won't eat, I will.

199
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:39,280
Baozhu's still laid up in bed,

200
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:41,480
and you're in the mood
for this little performance?

201
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:43,680
Go on, eat as much as you like.

202
00:15:44,120 --> 00:15:45,120
At least it'll shut you up.

203
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:46,200
Yan,

204
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:49,400
it's one thing to snub Xi and me
day after day.

205
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:51,720
But Father's done nothing to you!

206
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:52,800
Qiao!

207
00:15:53,400 --> 00:15:57,680
Then ask him how I hurt my legs.

208
00:16:01,400 --> 00:16:02,880
Weren't you riding with Father

209
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:04,080
when you fell off and hurt your legs?

210
00:16:04,160 --> 00:16:06,440
Yes. Didn't you just fall off by accident?

211
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:09,240
Enough, Xi.
Stop fighting with your brother.

212
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:10,320
I…

213
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:27,680
Yan, you…

214
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:43,120
Help your brother.

215
00:16:43,320 --> 00:16:44,320
-Sit down and eat,
-Yan.

216
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:46,000
Sit.

217
00:16:57,280 --> 00:16:58,920
Who could put up with that temper?

218
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:02,400
-What did you say?
-Enough. Eat.

219
00:17:03,680 --> 00:17:04,680
Let's eat.

220
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:05,800
Eat up.

221
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:23,160
You're spending the night here?

222
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:27,800
You can go.

223
00:17:28,720 --> 00:17:30,280
What about Lady Jin?

224
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:35,360
Actually, one of the matrons
gave me a little booklet.

225
00:17:39,800 --> 00:17:40,800
Gently.

226
00:17:40,960 --> 00:17:41,960
All right.

227
00:18:48,320 --> 00:18:49,320
Thank you.

228
00:18:51,360 --> 00:18:52,360
Jin Baozhu.

229
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:04,880
Left, right.

230
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:08,360
Left foot, right foot.

231
00:20:09,920 --> 00:20:12,240
Left foot, right foot.

232
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:15,800
Left, right foot.

233
00:20:17,280 --> 00:20:19,240
Left foot, right foot.

234
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:20,320
Xie Yan.

235
00:20:21,200 --> 00:20:22,920
Which story are we acting out today?

236
00:20:23,520 --> 00:20:25,800
We're chasing dogs today.

237
00:20:27,240 --> 00:20:29,160
Didn't you say that in this courtyard,

238
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:31,680
any word about legs was forbidden?

239
00:20:32,120 --> 00:20:33,800
Today I'm saying every last one!

240
00:20:33,920 --> 00:20:35,520
I run! I jump!

241
00:20:35,680 --> 00:20:37,320
-I kick! I leap!
-I pace!

242
00:20:37,440 --> 00:20:39,640
I stride! I walk like I'm flying!

243
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:40,880
I leap wherever I please!

244
00:20:41,080 --> 00:20:42,320
I climb mountains! Cross rivers!

245
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:43,640
Like it's a stroll in the park!

246
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:45,080
I push off!

247
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:48,040
I spring up!
And sail over Golden Dragon Gate!

248
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:55,920
I'm hungry.
I want dragon liver and phoenix marrow!

249
00:20:56,040 --> 00:20:57,920
Sea cucumber and shark fin,
abalone and fish maw!

250
00:20:58,440 --> 00:20:59,880
Ready to eat, Your Majesty?

251
00:21:01,320 --> 00:21:02,880
If you haven't got either,

252
00:21:03,480 --> 00:21:07,040
could I have a plum drink with honey?

253
00:21:07,120 --> 00:21:09,840
Preferably from the ice cellar,
chilled overnight.

254
00:21:10,520 --> 00:21:11,760
Still want your cakes?

255
00:21:11,840 --> 00:21:12,840
Yes! Yes!

256
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:15,720
A bag of osmanthus cakes,
freshly steamed, please.

257
00:21:16,720 --> 00:21:18,120
It's only the third lunar month.

258
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:19,880
Where am I supposed to get osmanthus?

259
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:22,920
I'm still ill, you know.

260
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:25,800
A few little requests,
and you can't take it?

261
00:21:26,040 --> 00:21:28,120
I think you're the one
who wants to be emperor!

262
00:21:31,520 --> 00:21:34,120
<i>Back in those days</i>

263
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:38,080
<i>Proud and fierce upon my dappled horse</i>

264
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:42,320
<i>Enemy blood upon my scarlet skirt</i>

265
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:52,560
Eat.

266
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:08,520
He's been spoiled all his life.

267
00:22:08,600 --> 00:22:10,480
Only you, my lady,
can get him to do a thing.

268
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:14,000
What are you staring at?

269
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:16,880
His Majesty.

270
00:22:19,960 --> 00:22:21,760
The Xie ancestral hall

271
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:31,680
Yan's legs

272
00:22:32,520 --> 00:22:34,320
are finally getting better.

273
00:22:35,120 --> 00:22:38,720
Everything's well at home now.

274
00:22:39,840 --> 00:22:41,200
I wonder

275
00:22:44,600 --> 00:22:46,400
if you're at peace now.

276
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:16,560
Hanzhang

277
00:23:16,800 --> 00:23:18,480
It's been 24 years.

278
00:23:20,920 --> 00:23:26,440
Why have the Xies
never acknowledged her as family?

279
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:29,080
She met an untimely end.

280
00:23:30,120 --> 00:23:31,400
The rites should be simple.

281
00:23:40,760 --> 00:23:41,760
<i>Careful.</i>

282
00:23:44,160 --> 00:23:47,240
<i>Hanzhang, come here.</i>

283
00:23:50,400 --> 00:23:51,400
<i>Mother.</i>

284
00:23:53,520 --> 00:23:54,520
<i>My lord.</i>

285
00:23:55,480 --> 00:23:56,680
She's gone.

286
00:23:57,520 --> 00:23:59,120
Don't wear yourself out grieving.

287
00:24:00,280 --> 00:24:03,200
You should get some rest.

288
00:25:08,360 --> 00:25:10,760
Virtue sustains all things

289
00:25:19,040 --> 00:25:20,320
You're here late.

290
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:22,520
Were you visiting your mother?

291
00:25:24,720 --> 00:25:25,720
I was.

292
00:25:29,320 --> 00:25:31,920
My respects, Grandmother.

293
00:25:33,400 --> 00:25:34,400
Come, sit down.

294
00:25:35,640 --> 00:25:36,640
Thank you, Grandmother.

295
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:41,920
How are your legs?

296
00:25:45,280 --> 00:25:48,080
I can walk a little, but I'm slow.

297
00:25:48,680 --> 00:25:50,200
I still need daily practice.

298
00:25:52,040 --> 00:25:54,720
Well? You came here especially.

299
00:25:55,280 --> 00:25:57,840
Something on your mind?

300
00:25:58,320 --> 00:25:59,920
You know me so well, Grandmother,

301
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:02,200
so I'll get to the point.

302
00:26:10,920 --> 00:26:14,280
I owe my recovery entirely to Baozhu.

303
00:26:14,920 --> 00:26:16,040
You taught me,

304
00:26:16,720 --> 00:26:19,200
"Give without keeping score.
Never forget a kindness."

305
00:26:20,480 --> 00:26:23,080
So I ask for your permission

306
00:26:23,920 --> 00:26:25,640
to make Jin Baozhu my principal wife.

307
00:26:29,320 --> 00:26:30,760
Baozhu has done us a great service.

308
00:26:31,520 --> 00:26:33,920
She'll be well rewarded.

309
00:26:34,680 --> 00:26:38,520
But making her your principal wife,
isn't appropriate.

310
00:26:39,280 --> 00:26:41,120
You're a legitimate Xie grandson.

311
00:26:41,280 --> 00:26:43,840
You can't marry just anyone.

312
00:26:44,520 --> 00:26:46,840
She risked her life for the family.

313
00:26:47,240 --> 00:26:50,160
You must make sacrifices for it, too.

314
00:26:51,200 --> 00:26:54,720
Otherwise,
all her efforts will have been wasted.

315
00:26:57,320 --> 00:26:58,720
Since you mean to reward her,

316
00:27:00,040 --> 00:27:01,400
there's something else I'd like to ask.

317
00:27:05,240 --> 00:27:07,840
You mean Madam's ordered

318
00:27:08,200 --> 00:27:09,400
that at next month's ancestral ceremony,

319
00:27:09,600 --> 00:27:11,080
she's to cast the divination blocks?

320
00:27:11,200 --> 00:27:12,320
Not just that.

321
00:27:12,720 --> 00:27:14,400
She can wear a red ribbon in her hair!

322
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:18,120
I hear Yan went to Madam
and asked her himself.

323
00:27:18,200 --> 00:27:20,320
He asked for money and shops,

324
00:27:20,480 --> 00:27:23,160
and even for that Song fellow's
letter of recommendation.

325
00:27:24,120 --> 00:27:28,320
Madam refused
and sent him off with some money.

326
00:27:28,400 --> 00:27:29,800
Can she even run a shop?

327
00:27:29,880 --> 00:27:31,400
That's what Madam asked.

328
00:27:31,880 --> 00:27:33,080
Yan had nothing to say to that.

329
00:27:33,760 --> 00:27:35,640
Before he left, he took

330
00:27:35,720 --> 00:27:37,360
a hefty silver reward from family funds,

331
00:27:37,480 --> 00:27:39,480
and a full set of gold jewelry!

332
00:27:39,600 --> 00:27:40,600
Honestly!

333
00:27:42,080 --> 00:27:45,760
Whatever Madam decides,
just do as she says.

334
00:27:46,560 --> 00:27:50,920
Dressing up in red and green
is a principal wife's privilege.

335
00:27:51,880 --> 00:27:53,680
Yet she's been allowed to!

336
00:27:54,320 --> 00:27:58,000
Is Madam planning
to make her the principal wife?

337
00:27:58,520 --> 00:28:00,720
A principal wife must be a proper match.

338
00:28:01,560 --> 00:28:03,360
Madam wouldn't do that.

339
00:28:07,280 --> 00:28:09,400
And casting blocks in the ancestral hall?

340
00:28:09,760 --> 00:28:12,480
Only someone who's done the family
a great service gets that honor.

341
00:28:12,880 --> 00:28:13,880
She doesn't deserve it!

342
00:28:14,720 --> 00:28:16,960
Why is she the one chosen this year?

343
00:28:17,400 --> 00:28:18,800
What gives her the right?

344
00:28:19,320 --> 00:28:20,840
Because...

345
00:28:21,960 --> 00:28:25,400
she truly cares about Yan,
and about this family.

346
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:27,400
Don't we all?

347
00:28:28,200 --> 00:28:29,400
Don't you and I?

348
00:28:30,360 --> 00:28:31,960
And my two children?

349
00:28:32,480 --> 00:28:34,560
They fight over one thing, then the next.

350
00:28:35,880 --> 00:28:37,520
And your Yi?

351
00:28:38,600 --> 00:28:42,200
Tell me,
even if you won't think of yourself,

352
00:28:42,520 --> 00:28:44,160
what about your child?

353
00:28:46,800 --> 00:28:48,760
Look at me. I'm always ill.

354
00:28:49,400 --> 00:28:51,080
I can barely look after him.

355
00:28:51,720 --> 00:28:55,400
Yi's caught a cold,
and I don't dare go near him.

356
00:28:56,480 --> 00:28:57,920
I'm afraid I'd pass something on.

357
00:29:00,720 --> 00:29:02,240
When the master came back recently,

358
00:29:02,320 --> 00:29:03,680
he brought a little datura,

359
00:29:04,000 --> 00:29:05,600
for me to share among the courtyards.

360
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:08,320
It's very good for colds.

361
00:29:16,200 --> 00:29:17,320
Have you handed it out?

362
00:29:18,400 --> 00:29:21,080
I've been so busy,
I haven't had a moment to myself.

363
00:29:21,160 --> 00:29:22,520
When would I have had the chance?

364
00:29:23,000 --> 00:29:26,080
They say this medicine
is hard to get, even with money.

365
00:29:26,880 --> 00:29:29,480
Just the tiniest bit works wonders.

366
00:29:29,760 --> 00:29:32,200
But you must never
mix it with other medicines.

367
00:29:32,360 --> 00:29:34,800
The wrong combination
could be very serious.

368
00:29:49,280 --> 00:29:50,320
It's really for me?

369
00:29:51,440 --> 00:29:52,880
Is it pure gold?

370
00:29:53,200 --> 00:29:54,880
I heard gold's very soft.

371
00:29:56,440 --> 00:29:58,040
Pure gold wouldn't survive you.

372
00:29:58,280 --> 00:29:59,440
It's gold over iron.

373
00:30:04,960 --> 00:30:07,240
Here. Let me put it on you.

374
00:30:16,160 --> 00:30:17,160
Pretty?

375
00:30:21,720 --> 00:30:22,720
Beautiful.

376
00:30:23,600 --> 00:30:24,600
Prettier than Diaochan.

377
00:30:25,720 --> 00:30:28,080
Who's she?
When did you meet her?

378
00:30:35,520 --> 00:30:37,920
Where were you last night?
You came back so late.

379
00:30:41,160 --> 00:30:42,720
Last night...

380
00:30:43,560 --> 00:30:45,000
was the anniversary
of my mother's death.

381
00:30:48,200 --> 00:30:49,200
She died young.

382
00:30:50,120 --> 00:30:51,280
For as long as I can remember,

383
00:30:51,840 --> 00:30:53,840
it was my stepmother
who raised me on her own.

384
00:30:54,920 --> 00:30:56,320
But I never felt alone.

385
00:30:56,920 --> 00:30:58,400
Mother left me so much.

386
00:30:59,400 --> 00:31:00,640
When I got into trouble as a child,

387
00:31:01,200 --> 00:31:02,400
kneeling alone as punishment,

388
00:31:03,880 --> 00:31:05,520
I'd trace these stitches

389
00:31:05,600 --> 00:31:07,720
and think about all sorts of things.

390
00:31:14,840 --> 00:31:16,040
It's beautiful embroidery.

391
00:31:17,080 --> 00:31:18,440
It must have taken so long.

392
00:31:18,840 --> 00:31:20,080
She must have loved you very much.

393
00:31:21,520 --> 00:31:22,680
But I keep wondering

394
00:31:25,280 --> 00:31:26,640
whether she was lonely.

395
00:31:37,880 --> 00:31:39,440
Why daylilies?

396
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:42,320
They're said to take your worries away.

397
00:31:42,840 --> 00:31:44,800
That's why we call them
"forget-your-worries flowers."

398
00:31:46,800 --> 00:31:48,520
The ancestral ceremony's coming up.

399
00:31:49,040 --> 00:31:50,920
And here in this house,
a lot of people are watching us.

400
00:31:51,520 --> 00:31:52,920
Keep your eyes open, whatever you do.
